Feature: The tool is called tminus, and gdd is another name for it
  The method is still GDD, Gate-Driven Development; the tool that runs it is now called tminus.
  The command tminus and the command gdd are the same program: each says its own name when asked
  for its version or its help, and every other message names tminus. A new project keeps its
  files in tminus/ and its state in .tminus/, its agents' commands are called tminus-<command>,
  and the variables tminus reads and sets start with TMINUS_. A project set up before the rename,
  with gdd/ and .gdd/, keeps working as it is: tminus reads and writes those folders and moves
  nothing. A variable that starts with TMINUS_ comes first; the same one with GDD_ still works.
  A folder with both kinds of project is refused, so no state is ever read from the wrong one.

  Scenario Outline: The tool says its own name with its version
    Given an empty folder
    When I run "<name> --version"
    Then it succeeds
    And the output contains "<name> 0."

    Examples:
      | name   |
      | tminus |
      | gdd    |

  Scenario Outline: The help names the tool as it was called and the method GDD
    Given an empty folder
    When I run "<name> --help"
    Then it succeeds
    And the output contains "Usage: <name> [COMMAND]"
    And the output contains "GDD · Gate-Driven Development"

    Examples:
      | name   |
      | tminus |
      | gdd    |

  Scenario: Called as gdd, the other messages still name tminus
    Given an empty folder
    When the role "builder-build" runs "gdd launch c1"
    Then it fails with a message that contains "Agents that tminus started cannot run tminus launch"

  Scenario: A new project gets the new names, and its agents learn the method GDD from tminus
    Given an empty folder
    When I run "tminus init --name Notes --platform cli --stack rust --agents claude codex"
    Then it succeeds
    And the last commit on main says "tminus init"
    And the file "tminus/project.toml" exists
    And the file "tminus/commands.toml" exists
    And the file ".gitignore" contains ".tminus/"
    And the file ".github/workflows/tminus.yml" contains "run: tminus ci"
    And the file ".github/workflows/tminus.yml" contains "github.com/MarsGotta/gdd --tag"
    And the file ".claude/skills/tminus-build/SKILL.md" contains "name: tminus-build"
    And the file ".agents/skills/tminus-review/SKILL.md" exists
    And the file "AGENTS.md" contains "**GDD · Gate-Driven Development**"
    And the file "AGENTS.md" contains "`tminus` runs the gates"
    And the file "gdd" does not exist
    And the file ".claude/skills/gdd-build/SKILL.md" does not exist

  Scenario: A project set up before the rename keeps its folders and keeps working
    Given an empty folder
    And the file "gdd/project.toml" says:
      """
      name = "Notes"
      language = "en"
      """
    And the file "gdd/zones.toml" says:
      """
      default = "yellow"
      """
    And the folder is a git repository with the file "README.md"
    When I run "tminus new-change c1 --title Export --paths src/app.txt"
    Then it succeeds
    And the file ".gdd/changes/c1/change.json" exists
    And the file "gdd/project.toml" exists
    And the file ".tminus" does not exist
    And the file "tminus" does not exist

  Scenario: A project set up before the rename keeps the gdd names of its agents' commands
    Given an empty folder
    And the file "gdd/project.toml" says:
      """
      name = "Notes"
      language = "en"
      """
    When I run "tminus agents install --agent claude"
    Then it succeeds
    And the file ".claude/skills/gdd-build/SKILL.md" contains "name: gdd-build"
    And the file ".claude/skills/gdd-build/SKILL.md" contains "Generated by `gdd agents install`"
    And the file ".claude/skills/tminus-build/SKILL.md" does not exist

  Scenario: A TMINUS_ variable comes first
    Given a GDD project in a git repository with the protected paths:
      """
      [protected]
      all = ["tminus/**"]
      """
    And the zone map:
      """
      default = "yellow"

      [[zone]]
      color = "green"
      paths = ["docs/**"]
      """
    And everything is committed on main
    And I run "tminus new-change c1 --title Docs --paths docs/a.md"
    And I run "tminus new-change c2 --title Menu --paths src/menu.txt"
    And the environment has "GDD_CHANGE" set to "c1"
    And the environment has "TMINUS_CHANGE" set to "c2"
    When I run "tminus classify"
    Then it succeeds
    And the JSON field "color" is "yellow"

  Scenario: A GDD_ variable still works without its TMINUS_ twin
    Given a GDD project in a git repository with the protected paths:
      """
      [protected]
      all = ["tminus/**"]
      """
    And the zone map:
      """
      default = "yellow"

      [[zone]]
      color = "green"
      paths = ["docs/**"]
      """
    And everything is committed on main
    And I run "tminus new-change c1 --title Docs --paths docs/a.md"
    And the environment has "GDD_CHANGE" set to "c1"
    When I run "tminus classify"
    Then it succeeds
    And the JSON field "color" is "green"

  Scenario: An agent started with its role in TMINUS_ROLE is refused like one in GDD_ROLE
    Given an empty folder
    And the environment has "TMINUS_ROLE" set to "reviewer"
    When I run "tminus adopt"
    Then it fails with a message that contains "Agents that tminus started cannot run tminus adopt"

  Scenario: A folder with both kinds of project is refused
    Given an empty folder
    And the file "tminus/project.toml" says:
      """
      name = "Notes"
      language = "en"
      """
    And the file "gdd/project.toml" says:
      """
      name = "Notes"
      language = "en"
      """
    When I run "tminus status"
    Then it fails with a message that contains "both tminus/project.toml and gdd/project.toml"
